course: dictionary
lesson: 15256
title: Showy
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Showy is a describing word. It means very bright, big or colourful, so that people notice it. «The garden was full of showy red poppies.» You can see the poppies from across the garden, so showy means eye-catching.
explain: Showy can also mean something done to make people admire you, not for a real purpose. «He did a showy trick on his bike just to make his friends clap.» The trick was not needed to ride the bike; he wanted to be watched.
explain: Showy can praise or criticise. «The showy flowers were pink and white» sounds happy, but «Mia's showy hat was too much for school» is a complaint. The clues are the words around it: the feeling in the sentence tells you which one is meant.
fact: Showy means very bright, big or colourful, so that people notice it.
fact: Showy can also mean done to make people admire you, rather than for a real purpose.
fact: Showy flowers have large, bright petals that attract bees.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad loves showy things, such as his gaudy caravan and loud clothes.
fact: The word can be a warning as well as praise, as in «too showy».
exercise: «The garden was full of showy red poppies.» What does showy mean here? | *Very bright and easy to notice | Quiet and hidden under the leaves | Small and grey | Cold to touch
exercise: «He did a showy trick on his bike just to make his friends clap.» Why did he do the trick? | To keep dry in the rain | To fix his bike | To get home more quickly | *To be seen and admired
exercise: Ben says, «The car has too many showy lights.» What does Ben think about the lights? | They are broken and need mending | *They are too bright and noticeable | They are switched off and hard to see | They are the right amount for night driving
test: «Mia wore a showy hat with bright feathers to the party.» Mia's hat is showy because it is | Old and torn | *Bright and noticeable, perhaps a bit too much | Hidden under her coat | Plain and grey
test: «Showy flowers have large, bright petals that attract bees.» Why are the petals of showy flowers useful to the plant? | *They attract bees, which help the plant | They make the stem grow taller | They help the flower hide from bees | They keep the rain off the stem
exam: Which sentence uses showy to criticise someone? | The showy bird sang loudly in the tree | The showy flowers made the garden look bright | The showy sunset over the sea was beautiful | *Her showy trick was only done to make everyone look at her
